g#adj:0"},"raw":{"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"So zu reden wie du, ist kein Kunststück; du verfährst gerade wie jener Herr bei Dickens, der alle schwierigen Fragen mit der linken Hand über die rechte Schulter wirft.","ref":"1913 [1878], chapter 11, in Hermann Röhl, transl., Anna Karenina, translation of Анна Каренина (Anna Karenina) by Leo Tolstoy, part 1:","english":"It's very well for you to talk like that; it's very much like that gentleman in Dickens who used to fling all difficult questions over his right shoulder.","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[98,109]],"translation":"It's very well for you to talk like that; it's very much like that gentleman in Dickens who used to fling all difficult questions over his right shoulder.","bold_translation_offsets":[[110,119]]},{"text":"Die Frühdiagnose ist schwierig, – zumal für die Herren Kollegen im Flachland.","ref":"1924, Thomas Mann, Der Zauberberg [The Magic Mountain], volume 1, Berlin: S. Fischer, page 306; republished as Helen T. Lowe-Porter, transl., The Magic Mountain, 1927:","english":"The early diagnosis is very difficult—particularly for my colleagues down below[.]","type":"quotation","translation":"The early diagnosis is very difficult—particularly for my colleagues down below[.]","bold_text_offsets":[[21,30]],"bold_translation_offsets":[[28,37]]}],"links":[["difficult","difficult"],["hard","hard"],["challenging","challenging"],["tough","tough"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"schwer"}],"glosses":["difficult, hard, challenging, tough"],"categories":["German terms with quotations"]},{"examples":[{"text":"Iran wurde von den arabischen Golfländern so betrachtet wie Russland lange in Europa: ein schwieriger Nachbar, mit dem man sich aber irgendwie arrangieren muss.","ref":"2026 April 21, Lisa Schneider, “Feuerpause im Irankrieg: Vor der nächsten Kriegsrunde?”, in Die Tageszeitung: taz, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[90,101]]}],"links":[["difficult","difficult"],["prickly","prickly"]],"categories"